  "articleBody": "Buying a foreclosed property can be exciting, but these homes often come with a unique set of challenges. Knowing when to bring in a pro for repairs can save you a lot of headaches and money down the line. Structural damage is a big one — if you see cracks in the foundation, sagging floors, or a compromised roof, that's definitely a job for a licensed contractor. Electrical issues, like frayed wiring or outdated panels, aren't just an inconvenience; they're a serious safety hazard. Same goes for plumbing problems; a burst pipe can lead to massive water damage and mold growth if not addressed quickly and correctly. And speaking of mold, if you spot any significant growth, especially in damp areas, you'll want to call in mold remediators. Finally, if any repair affects the home's safety or code compliance, a qualified professional is your best bet. We've seen it all, from minor fixes to major overhauls, and getting expert help ensures the work is done right and stands the test of time. Don't hesitate to reach out if you're unsure about the extent of damage or the best way to tackle it.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
